WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.014 --> 00:00:03.350
INTERIM BASIS.

00:00:02.015 --> 00:00:05.285
IT COULD BE MONTHS BEFORE

00:00:03.483 --> 00:00:05.585
JACKSON IS CONFIRMED.

00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:07.187
BRET?

00:00:05.719 --> 00:00:10.257
&gt;&gt; Bret: LUCAS, THANK YOU.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.590
LET'S HEAR DIRECTLY NOW FROM DR.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.157
SHULKIN.

00:00:10.724 --> 00:00:12.626
HE JOINS US.

00:00:11.291 --> 00:00:12.926
MR. SECRETARY, THANKS FOR BEING

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:15.428
HERE.

00:00:13.059 --> 00:00:16.796
&gt;&gt; GLAD TO BE HERE, BRET.

00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:17.097
&gt;&gt; Bret: SO LET'S START WITH

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.432
THIS.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.101
WHY DO YOU THINK YOU WERE FIRED?

00:00:19.566 --> 00:00:22.369
&gt;&gt; WELL, EVERY CABINET MEMBER

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:22.736
SERVES AT THE PLEASURE OF THE

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:24.137
PRESIDENT.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:25.038
AND IT'S THE PRESIDENT'S

00:00:24.271 --> 00:00:26.339
PREROGATIVE TO HAVE A TEAM

00:00:25.171 --> 00:00:26.973
AROUND HIM THAT HE THINKS IS

00:00:26.473 --> 00:00:29.142
DOING THE JOB.

00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:30.143
I THINK WE HEARD TODAY FROM THE

00:00:29.276 --> 00:00:30.944
PRESIDENT THAT HE WASN'T HAPPY

00:00:30.277 --> 00:00:33.480
WITH THE PACE.

00:00:31.077 --> 00:00:33.847
AND, YOU KNOW, I AGREE WITH THE

00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:35.348
PRESIDENT.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.349
THIS IS AN ORGANIZATION THAT

00:00:35.482 --> 00:00:37.584
NEEDS TO CHANGE.

00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:39.619
IT NEEDS TO DO BETTER AT HIS JOB

00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:41.187
AND WE ALL WANT TO DO IT FASTER

00:00:39.753 --> 00:00:42.956
AND BETTER BECAUSE IT'S SO

00:00:41.321 --> 00:00:44.057
IMPORTANT TO THE COUNTRY.

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:45.692
AND I THINK THE PRESIDENT HAS

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.861
THE RIGHT TO HAVE THE SECRETARY

00:00:45.825 --> 00:00:49.429
THAT HE WANTS WITH HIM.

00:00:47.994 --> 00:00:50.764
&gt;&gt; Bret: YOU SAID THE

00:00:49.562 --> 00:00:52.132
ADMINISTRATION WANTS TO

00:00:50.897 --> 00:00:54.401
PRIVATIZE THE V.A.

00:00:52.265 --> 00:00:55.869
HAVE YOU EVER SEEN -- WE HAVEN'T

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:57.137
SEEN EVIDENCE AS FAR AS THE

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.707
SENT TO CONGRESS SAYING THAT.

00:00:59.072 --> 00:01:01.508
IS THERE ANY DIRECT

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.542
COMMUNICATION WITH CONGRESS THAT

00:01:01.641 --> 00:01:03.710
THE ADMINISTRATION WANTS TO

00:01:02.676 --> 00:01:06.446
PRIVATIZE THE V.A.?

00:01:03.843 --> 00:01:07.213
&gt;&gt; NO, BRET, I ACTUALLY HAVEN'T

00:01:06.579 --> 00:01:09.549
SAID THAT.

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:10.216
I WAS PART OF THE ADMINISTRATION

00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:11.518
UNTIL YESTERDAY.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.453
WE ARE NOT TRYING TO PRIVATIZE

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:14.921
THE V.A.

00:01:13.586 --> 00:01:15.789
WE ARE TRYING TO IMPROVE AND

00:01:15.055 --> 00:01:18.792
TRANSFORM THE V.A.

00:01:15.922 --> 00:01:20.627
WHAT I SAID IN MY EDITORIAL IS

00:01:18.925 --> 00:01:22.562
THAT THERE ARE A NUMBER OF

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.231
POLITICAL APPOINTEES WITHIN V.A.

00:01:22.696 --> 00:01:28.201
THAT ARE PUSHING TO PRIVATIZE

00:01:25.365 --> 00:01:29.336
MUCH FASTER THAN I THINK IS IN

00:01:28.335 --> 00:01:31.371
THE INTEREST OF A SAFE WAY TO

00:01:29.469 --> 00:01:33.139
CARE FOR OUR VETERANS AND I'VE

00:01:31.504 --> 00:01:34.741
STOOD UP FOR THEM BECAUSE I WAS

00:01:33.273 --> 00:01:35.775
IN WASHINGTON AND I WAS WORKING

00:01:34.874 --> 00:01:39.112
FOR THE PRESIDENT ON BEHALF OF

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:40.714
OUR VETERANS.

00:01:39.245 --> 00:01:43.883
&gt;&gt; Bret: WHY DID YOU FEEL THE

00:01:40.847 --> 00:01:45.618
NEED TO WRITE THE OP ED?

00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:47.253
&gt;&gt; LISTEN, I CAME TO WASHINGTON

00:01:45.752 --> 00:01:48.488
FROM THE PRIVATE SECTOR FOR ONE

00:01:47.387 --> 00:01:49.656
REASON TO FIX THE V.A.

00:01:48.621 --> 00:01:50.023
I KNOW THIS MATTERS A LOT TO THE

00:01:49.789 --> 00:01:51.391
PRESIDENT.

00:01:50.156 --> 00:01:52.993
AND WE, AS A COUNTRY, HAVE A

00:01:51.524 --> 00:01:53.626
LONG WAY TO GO TO GET THE V.A.

00:01:53.126 --> 00:01:56.863
IN PROPER SHAPE.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:58.131
BUT IT WOULD BE A MISTAKE TO

00:01:56.997 --> 00:01:59.232
CONCLUDE THAT WE DO NOT NEED THE

00:01:58.264 --> 00:02:00.600
V.A. AND THAT WE HAVE TO

00:01:59.366 --> 00:02:01.901
DISMANTLE THE V.A.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.370
WE HAVE TO IMPROVE THE V.A.

00:02:02.035 --> 00:02:05.171
WHILE AT THE SAME TIME, WORKING

00:02:03.503 --> 00:02:05.972
WITH THE PRIVATE SECTOR IN

00:02:05.305 --> 00:02:08.375
INTEGRATED WAY TO MEET THE NEEDS

00:02:06.106 --> 00:02:10.143
OF OUR VETERANS.

00:02:08.508 --> 00:02:12.712
&gt;&gt; Bret: YOU KNOW, WE HEARD THIS

00:02:10.276 --> 00:02:14.814
SOUNDBITE IN LUCAS' PIECE FROM

00:02:12.846 --> 00:02:16.549
SENATOR MORAN QUESTIONING YOUR

00:02:14.948 --> 00:02:17.217
DEALINGS WITH THAT PARTICULAR

00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:17.984
COMMITTEE.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.552
DID YOU HAVE A CREDIBILITY ISSUE

00:02:18.118 --> 00:02:20.653
WITH CONGRESS?

00:02:19.686 --> 00:02:22.355
&gt;&gt; OH, I DON'T THINK SO.

00:02:20.787 --> 00:02:25.992
YOU HAVE TO REMEMBER, I'M THE

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:26.559
ONLY CABINET MEMBER THAT HAD

00:02:26.126 --> 00:02:28.728
100-0 VOTE.

00:02:26.693 --> 00:02:29.195
I PRIDED MYSELF IN WORKING IN A

00:02:28.862 --> 00:02:32.132
BIPARTISAN WAY.

00:02:29.329 --> 00:02:34.601
SENATOR MORAN FELT STRONGLY

00:02:32.265 --> 00:02:36.836
ABOUT PUSHING TO GIVE VETERANS

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:38.071
ADDITIONAL OPTIONS THAT,

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.973
FRANKLY, HIS OWN SENATORS, THE

00:02:38.204 --> 00:02:42.075
COMMITTEE DIDN'T AGREE WITH.

00:02:40.106 --> 00:02:43.410
HE LOST HIS AMENDMENT 14-1.

00:02:42.208 --> 00:02:43.843
HE WAS THE ONLY ONE VOTING

00:02:43.543 --> 00:02:45.145
AGAINST IT.

00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:46.913
AND HE WAS FRUSTRATED BY THAT.

00:02:45.278 --> 00:02:48.681
BY THE WAY, YOU KNOW, HE HAD

00:02:47.047 --> 00:02:50.083
SOME REASONABLE POINTS THERE.

00:02:48.815 --> 00:02:52.252
SO THERE ARE MANY THINGS THAT HE

00:02:50.216 --> 00:02:53.353
AND I AGREED UPON BUT IN THE

00:02:52.385 --> 00:02:56.156
END, HE DIDN'T LIKE THE POSITION

00:02:53.486 --> 00:02:57.057
THAT I TOOK WHICH WAS TO DO WHAT

00:02:56.289 --> 00:03:00.193
I THOUGHT WAS THE RIGHT THING

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:02.829
FOR OUR VETERANS.

00:03:00.326 --> 00:03:04.297
&gt;&gt; Bret: ABOUT 11 MONTHS AGO, I

00:03:02.962 --> 00:03:05.632
HAD YOU ON "SPECIAL REPORT" AND

00:03:04.431 --> 00:03:06.399
WE WERE TALKING ABOUT THE

00:03:05.765 --> 00:03:06.866
CHALLENGES.

00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:07.534
TAKE A LISTEN.

00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:10.570
ARE YOU SEEING CHANGE?

00:03:09.369 --> 00:03:12.338
&gt;&gt; WE'RE IN THE INTENSIVE CARE

00:03:10.703 --> 00:03:13.006
UNIT AND WE'RE MONITORING THINGS

00:03:12.472 --> 00:03:15.675
REALLY CLOSELY.

00:03:13.139 --> 00:03:16.643
BUT I AM OPTIMISTIC THAT WE'RE

00:03:15.809 --> 00:03:18.344
BEGINNING TO FINALLY DEAL WITH

00:03:16.776 --> 00:03:21.081
THE ISSUES THAT HAVE PLAGUED THE

00:03:18.478 --> 00:03:22.549
V.A. SYSTEM FOR DECADES.

00:03:21.214 --> 00:03:24.951
&gt;&gt; Bret: SO THE PRESIDENT SAID

00:03:22.682 --> 00:03:27.053
TODAY THAT HE JUST WASN'T HAPPY

00:03:25.085 --> 00:03:27.353
HOW FAST OR HOW THINGS WERE

00:03:27.187 --> 00:03:28.922
GOING.

00:03:27.487 --> 00:03:31.191
THAT THEY WERE GOING TOO SLOWLY.

00:03:29.055 --> 00:03:32.625
WHAT'S YOUR RESPONSE TO THAT AND

00:03:31.324 --> 00:03:33.126
WHAT CAN BE DONE TO CHANGE THAT

00:03:32.759 --> 00:03:34.427
PACE?

00:03:33.259 --> 00:03:36.162
&gt;&gt; WELL, I DON'T THINK THE

00:03:34.561 --> 00:03:37.664
PRESIDENT SHOULD BE HAPPY WITH

00:03:36.296 --> 00:03:38.832
WHERE WE WERE, AND AS SECRETARY,

00:03:37.797 --> 00:03:39.132
I WASN'T HAPPY WITH WHERE WE

00:03:38.965 --> 00:03:40.633
WERE.

00:03:39.265 --> 00:03:43.103
WE HAVE TO FIGURE OUT HOW TO

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:46.172
MOVE THIS BUREAUCRACY FASTER AND

00:03:43.236 --> 00:03:48.308
BE MORE RESPONSIVE.

00:03:46.306 --> 00:03:49.576
WHEN YOU SHOWED THEM, I KNOW

00:03:48.441 --> 00:03:50.443
THEM VERY WELL AND, FRANKLY,

00:03:49.709 --> 00:03:53.713
THIS WAS A SYSTEM THAT FAILED

00:03:50.577 --> 00:03:54.013
THEM AND WE SHOULDN'T BE DOING

00:03:53.847 --> 00:03:55.915
THAT.

00:03:54.147 --> 00:03:56.716
THIS IS A SYSTEM THAT NEEDS TO

00:03:56.049 --> 00:03:57.784
BE PUSHED.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.085
MANY OF THE BUREAUCRATIC

00:03:57.917 --> 00:03:59.519
ELEMENTS NEED TO BE

00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:00.520
RESTRUCTURED.

00:03:59.652 --> 00:04:02.489
I'VE STARTED THAT PROCESS.

00:04:00.653 --> 00:04:03.256
I HOPE THAT DR. JACKSON WILL

00:04:02.622 --> 00:04:06.626
CONTINUE THAT PROCESS BECAUSE IT

00:04:03.389 --> 00:04:08.228
NEEDS TO BE DONE.

00:04:06.759 --> 00:04:09.496
&gt;&gt; Bret: YOU KNOW, YOU HAD THE

00:04:08.361 --> 00:04:12.132
INSPECTOR GENERAL, OBVIOUSLY,

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:13.266
COME OUT WITH THIS SCATHING

00:04:12.265 --> 00:04:13.600
REPORT ABOUT YOUR TRIP TO

00:04:13.399 --> 00:04:15.435
EUROPE.

00:04:13.733 --> 00:04:17.537
WE'VE BEEN OVER THAT.

00:04:15.568 --> 00:04:19.172
AND YOUR RESPONSE TO THAT.

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.206
WERE THERE OTHER I.G.

00:04:19.305 --> 00:04:21.574
INVESTIGATIONS OR AUDITS THAT

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:21.941
WE'RE FACTORING INTO THIS WHOLE

00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:23.510
THING?

00:04:22.075 --> 00:04:25.912
&gt;&gt; WELL, YOU KNOW, WASHINGTON IS

00:04:23.643 --> 00:04:27.280
A TOWN THAT THROWS UP ALL SORTS

00:04:26.045 --> 00:04:28.114
OF ALLEGATIONS.

00:04:27.413 --> 00:04:29.315
THERE WERE ALLEGATIONS OF

00:04:28.248 --> 00:04:30.250
ADDITIONAL REPORTS.

00:04:29.449 --> 00:04:31.918
BUT THERE HAVE BEEN NO OTHER

00:04:30.383 --> 00:04:32.819
REPORTS THAT HAVE COME OUT.

00:04:32.051 --> 00:04:35.355
AND I'VE ADDRESSED THAT

00:04:32.952 --> 00:04:38.525
EVERYTHING THAT I DID ON THIS

00:04:35.488 --> 00:04:38.858
EUROPEAN TRIP WAS PREAPPROVED BY

00:04:38.658 --> 00:04:39.993
ETHICS.

00:04:38.992 --> 00:04:41.161
WAS CONSISTENT WITH PAST

00:04:40.126 --> 00:04:42.028
POLICIES IN V.A. BUT WHEN THE

00:04:41.294 --> 00:04:43.997
INSPECTOR GENERAL HAD CONCERNS

00:04:42.162 --> 00:04:46.199
ABOUT IT, I WROTE A CHECK AND I

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:48.434
PAID BACK EVERY PENNY OF A

00:04:46.332 --> 00:04:49.335
SINGLE COACH AIR FARE.

00:04:48.568 --> 00:04:50.503
THAT WAS THE TOTAL AMOUNT THAT

00:04:49.469 --> 00:04:51.838
GOVERNMENT FUNDS WERE USED FOR.

00:04:50.637 --> 00:04:53.973
AND I PAID THAT BACK.

00:04:51.971 --> 00:04:54.274
SO LOOK, I THINK I'VE ADDRESSED

00:04:54.107 --> 00:04:57.810
THAT.

00:04:54.407 --> 00:04:59.913
THIS WAS USED IN A POLITICAL WAY

00:04:57.944 --> 00:05:01.514
TO TRY TO REMOVE ME.

00:05:00.046 --> 00:05:01.915
AND, YOU KNOW, THIS IS

00:05:01.648 --> 00:05:02.549
WASHINGTON.

00:05:02.048 --> 00:05:04.651
I'M A BIG BOY.

00:05:02.682 --> 00:05:06.419
I UNDERSTAND THAT.

00:05:04.784 --> 00:05:07.954
I'VE SAID THAT IT SHOULDN'T BE

00:05:06.553 --> 00:05:09.722
THIS HARD TO SERVE YOUR COUNTRY,

00:05:08.087 --> 00:05:11.257
AND I DON'T THINK IT SHOULD BE.

00:05:09.856 --> 00:05:14.928
BUT THANKFULLY, THERE WERE MANY

00:05:11.391 --> 00:05:19.032
PEOPLE THAT ARE STILL TRYING TO

00:05:15.061 --> 00:05:18.781
FIX

00:05:18.781 --> 00:05:22.502
FI

00:05:19.165 --> 00:05:23.369
FIX.

00:05:22.635 --> 00:05:24.504
&gt;&gt; Bret: SHE HAD HE GET

00:05:23.503 --> 00:05:25.772
CONFIRMED, WHAT WOULD IT BE?

00:05:24.637 --> 00:05:27.874
&gt;&gt; TO MAKE SURE THAT HE'S

00:05:25.905 --> 00:05:29.809
CONSISTENT WITH THE PRESIDENT'S

00:05:28.007 --> 00:05:31.678
AGENDA, TO PUSH REALLY HARD,

00:05:29.943 --> 00:05:34.781
ALWAYS TO KEEP THE VETERANS'

00:05:31.811 --> 00:05:38.451
INTEREST AT HEART.

00:05:34.914 --> 00:05:37.567
THAT MIKE

00:05:37.567 --> 00:05:37.750
THAT MIK

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:37.784
THAT MAK

00:05:37.784 --> 00:05:37.817
THAT MAKE

00:05:37.817 --> 00:05:37.850
THAT MAKE S

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:37.884
THAT MAKE SUR

00:05:37.884 --> 00:05:37.917
THAT MAKE SURE

00:05:37.917 --> 00:05:37.951
THAT MAKE SURE H

00:05:37.951 --> 00:05:37.984
THAT MAKE SURE HE'

00:05:37.984 --> 00:05:38.017
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S

00:05:38.017 --> 00:05:38.051
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S W

00:05:38.051 --> 00:05:38.084
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S WOR

00:05:38.084 --> 00:05:38.117
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S WORKI

00:05:38.117 --> 00:05:38.184
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S WORKING

00:05:38.184 --> 00:05:38.218
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S WORKING W

00:05:38.218 --> 00:05:38.251
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S WORKING WIT

00:05:38.251 --> 00:05:40.119
THAT MAKE SURE HE'S WORKING WITH

00:05:38.585 --> 00:05:42.288
CONGRESS IN A BIPARTISAN WAY AND

00:05:40.253 --> 00:05:43.022
MAKE SURE HE'S LISTENING TO THE

00:05:42.422 --> 00:05:44.023
VETERANS GROUPS.

00:05:43.156 --> 00:05:44.390
FRANKLY, THAT'S WHY WE'RE DOING

00:05:44.157 --> 00:05:45.959
THIS.

00:05:44.524 --> 00:05:46.793
THAT'S WHAT A RESPONSIVE

00:05:46.092 --> 00:05:47.994
ORGANIZATION NEEDS TO BE

00:05:46.926 --> 00:05:50.063
SUCCESSFUL IN DOING IS LISTENING

00:05:48.127 --> 00:05:51.898
TO THOSE THAT IT SERVES.

00:05:50.196 --> 00:05:53.266
SO I WILL HELP DR. JACKSON IN

00:05:52.031 --> 00:05:54.467
ANY WAY THAT HE NEEDS HELP,

00:05:53.399 --> 00:05:57.136
BECAUSE IT'S VERY IMPORTANT THAT

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:58.037
WE SUCCEED AT THIS MISSION.

